    "https://jobs.ucf.edu/jobs/senior-manager-real-estate-assets-operations-orlando-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Real Estate Assets & Operations",
      "description": "Senior Manager, Real Estate Assets & Operations - Orlando, Florida, United States University of Central Florida Navigation Home Meet Our People Featured Jobs Resources Faculty Join Our Talent Network Search Jobs Kiosk mode Senior Manager, Real Estate Assets & Operations Facilities (A&P) Skip to section BENEFITS WHY UCF? ABOUT ORLANDO My Profile Ready to Apply? Senior Manager, Real Estate Assets & Operations R114355 Main Campus, Orlando, Florida Staff Full time Closing at: Oct 15 2026 - 12:00am EDT Real Estate Office Add to favorites View favorites University Operations: University Operations at UCF is committed to creating a supportive and welcoming environment for our faculty, staff, students, and the broader community. We take pride in delivering exceptional service, sharing our expertise, and upholding the highest standards to ensure a world-class campus experience. Visit our website or follow us on Facebook and Instagram to learn more. The Opportunity : Under the direction of the Director of Real Estate and Property Management, the Senior Manager, Real Estate Assets and Operations is responsible for the strategic oversight, operational performance, financial performance, and long-term stewardship of an assigned portfolio of commercial, office, research, academic, mixed-use, and specialty real estate assets. The position develops and implements asset management strategies; oversees portfolio operations, financial performance, lease administration, capital planning, and stakeholder relationships; and provides leadership to ensure assets are managed in a manner that protects university interests, mitigates risk, maximizes value, and supports institutional objectives. Responsibilities: Manage the operational and strategic performance of an assigned real estate portfolio. Develop and implement asset management strategies that enhance asset value, operational effectiveness, occupant satisfaction, and long-term sustainability. Evaluate facility condition, operational risks, occupancy trends, service delivery, and portfolio performance metrics. Conduct property inspections and assessments and develop recommendations to address deficiencies, improve efficiency, mitigate risk, and optimize portfolio performance. Ensure compliance with university policies, lease requirements, regulatory obligations, and applicable building standards. Develop, administer, and monitor annual operating and capital budgets for assigned assets. Analyze financial performance, operating results, occupancy trends, revenue generation, recoveries, and expenses and develop recommendations to improve financial outcomes. Oversee forecasting, variance analysis, accounts receivable, reconciliations, CAM recoveries, operating expense management, and financial reporting. Monitor outstanding balances and implement strategies to improve collections and reduce financial risk. Ensure financial records and reporting are accurate, timely, and compliant with university procedures and reporting requirements. Present financial and operational performance information and recommendations to departmental leadership and stakeholders. Develop, prioritize, and recommend capital renewal, deferred maintenance, tenant improvement, and facility enhancement initiatives for the assigned portfolio. Evaluate facility condition assessments, operational requirements, asset life-cycle considerations, and stakeholder needs to establish capital priorities. Manage planning, budgeting, procurement, implementation, and performance monitoring of approved projects. Coordinate consultants, contractors, occupants, and university stakeholders to ensure projects are completed on schedule, within budget, and consistent with university objectives. Support development of long-term capital reserve and asset reinvestment strategies. Oversee lease administration activities for the assigned portfolio, including critical date tracking, compliance monitoring, operational requirements, rent escalations, renewals, amendments, assignments, insurance requirements, and reporting obligations. Support the Director and Real Estate Office in lease negotiations, acquisitions, dispositions, renewals, and other real estate transactions through analysis, documentation, due diligence, implementation, and stakeholder coordination Collaborate with legal counsel and university stakeholders regarding lease interpretation, compliance matters, and transaction documentation. Maintain accurate lease administration systems and records. Oversee contracted service providers and internal service delivery relationships supporting the portfolio. Develop scopes of work, procure services, administer contracts, evaluate vendor performance, and implement corrective actions when necessary. Manage relationships with property management, maintenance, landscaping, security, janitorial, construction, and specialty service providers. Ensure services are delivered in accordance with contractual requirements, performance standards, and university expectations. Provide leadership, direction, accountability, and performance oversight for assigned staff and supporting resources. Establish priorities, monitor workloads, evaluate performance, and promote professional development and continuous improvement. Build and maintain productive relationships with tenants, university leadership, faculty, staff, service providers, and external stakeholders. Lead efforts to improve operational processes, customer service, reporting, compliance, and portfolio management practices. Participate in strategic initiatives, policy development, and special projects supporting departmental and university objectives. Minimum Qualifications : Bachelors or Masters degree and 6+ years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219(6) . Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in Real Estate, Business Administration, Finance, Facilities Management, Construction Management, Public Administration, or a related field; advanced degree and relevant professional certifications preferred. Experience managing commercial real estate, property, facilities, or asset portfolios, including operational oversight and stakeholder engagement. Demonstrated experience with budgeting, financial analysis, forecasting, and performance reporting. Experience planning and managing capital improvement, renovation, deferred maintenance, or facility enhancement projects. Knowledge of lease administration, contract management, procurement, vendor management, and regulatory compliance. Strong leadership, project management, communication, analytical, and relationship-building skills, with experience working in higher education, public sector, or similarly complex organizations preferred. Special Instructions to the Applicants: The anticipated salary for a well-qualified candidate is between $89,076 and $133,614. The final determination of a successful candidate's starting salary will vary based on several factors, including education and relevant experience. The anticipated pay scale indicated for this position generally applies to candidates who meet the minimum requirements and several of the preferred qualifications outlined above. All offers are contingent on successful background and reference screens. Position requires a valid Class E driver’s license. The position may involve driving to various locations on and off campus to conduct University business. All applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position, and the university cannot accommodate H‑1B transfers or employment-based visa processing for individuals currently sponsored by another employer. Are you ready to unleash YOUR potential? As a next-generation public research university and Forbes-ranked top employer in Florida, we are a community of thinkers, doers, creators, innovators, healers, and leaders striving to create broader prosperity and help shape a better future. No matter what your role is, when you join Knight Nation, you’ll play an integral role at one of the most impactful universities in the country. You’ll be met with opportunities to connect and collaborate with talented faculty, staff, and students across 13 colleges and multiple campuses, engaging in impactful work that makes a positive difference. Your time at UCF will provide you with many meaningful opportunities to grow, you’ll work alongside talented colleagues on complex projects that will challenge you and help you gain new skills, and you’ll have countless rewarding experiences that go well beyond a paycheck. Working at UCF has its perks! UCF offers: Benefit packages, including Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending, and Employee Assistance Program Paid time off, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays Retirement savings options Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions Education assistance And more…For more benefits information, view the UCF Employee Benefits Guide . Dive into our Total Rewards Calculator to discover the diverse selection available to you, giving you a glimpse into the benefits that together shape your comprehensive rewards package at UCF. Unless explicitly stated on the job posting, it is UCF’s expectation that an employee of UCF will reside in Florida as of the date the employment begins. Department Facilities and Business Operations- Real Estate and Space Administration Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8 am to 5 pm, some afterhours Type of Appointment Regular Expected Salary $89,076.00 to Negotiable Job Posting End Date 10-15-2026-12-00-AM The University of Central Florida is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based on any characteristic protected by law.  The University maintains programs for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities in accordance with all applicable federal and state laws. As a Florida public university, the University of Central Florida makes all application materials and selection procedures available to the public upon request. UCF is proud to be a smoke-free campus and an E-Verify employer. For general application or posting questions, please email talent@ucf.edu . If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please email onac@ucf.edu . People Also Viewed Executive Director – NCTI Orlando Business Development and Partn (A&P) Information Security Professional IV, Lead Orlando Information Technology (A&P) Administrative Assistant II Orlando Administrative Management and (USPS) Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! First Name (required) a41c758d Last Name (required) 42f8120f Email (required) 3e644c53 Phone Number 0ed53179 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) D