    "https://jobs.ucf.edu/jobs/applications-programmer-v-orlando-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Applications Programmer V",
      "description": "Applications Programmer V - Orlando, Florida, United States University of Central Florida Navigation Home Meet Our People Featured Jobs Resources Faculty Join Our Talent Network Search Jobs Kiosk mode Applications Programmer V Information Technology (A&P) Skip to section BENEFITS WHY UCF? ABOUT ORLANDO My Profile Ready to Apply? Applications Programmer V R114346 Main Campus, Orlando, Florida Staff Full time Closing at: Oct 14 2026 - 12:00am EDT DCIO- ERP HR & Finance Systems Add to favorites View favorites University Operations: The University Operations division at UCF is committed to creating a supportive and welcoming environment for our faculty, staff, students, and the broader community. We take pride in delivering exceptional service, sharing our expertise, and upholding the highest standards to ensure a world-class campus experience. Visit our website or follow us on Facebook and Instagram to learn more. The Opportunity: University Operations is seeking to hire an Applications Programmer V. This role is responsible for leading designing, developing, implementing, and supporting enterprise Workday applications and integrations. This position serves as a technical expert responsible for driving complex integration projects, supporting critical business systems, and ensuring the reliability, performance, and continuous improvement of the university's Workday environment. Responsibilities: Lead the technical design, development, testing, deployment, and ongoing support of Workday applications, integrations, and related technologies. Serve as the primary technical resource for Workday integrations, collaborating with university ladership, functional teams, vendors, and external partners to support business operations. Design, develop, maintain, and enhance integrations between Workday, PeopleSoft, banking partners, and third-party applications. Manage Workday upgrades, environment management activities, and integration projects to ensure system stability and performance. Analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve complex application, integration, and data-related issues while implementing long-term solutions. Design and develop data conversion processes, application components, interfaces, reports, and custom software solutions. Create and maintain software integrations and external interfaces using technologies such as Workday Studio, Workday Orchestration, XML, web services, SQR, SQL, Java, and other integration tools. Lead programming activities including system design, coding, testing, debugging, and implementation of enterprise applications. Independently plan, organize, and coordinate complex data processing programs and systems, evaluating performance and recommending process improvements. Conduct technical research, data analysis, and special studies to support strategic initiatives and emerging business requirements. Manage multiple complex technical projects, including project planning, scheduling, coordination, and oversight of cross-functional teams and technical consultants. Provide technical guidance and consultation to university stakeholders, assisting in the resolution of system-related issues and supporting compliance with university policies and standards. Evaluate and recommend software enhancements, architecture improvements, and technology solutions to strengthen existing enterprise systems. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of relevant experience; or High School Diploma (or equivalent) and 9 years of relevant work experience in lieu of degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219(6) . Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and supporting Workday integrations across HCM, Finance, Payroll, and Student systems. Strong proficiency with Workday Studio, Workday Orchestrate, EIBs, Core Connectors, and web services. Experience integrating Workday with ERP, HRIS, financial, banking, and third-party vendor systems. Advanced programming experience with SQL, Java, XML, XSLT, and related technologies. Experience with data conversion, migration, and enterprise application integration projects. Strong project management and stakeholder engagement skills. Experience leading large-scale technical initiatives and mentoring technical team members. Excellent analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving abilities. Special Instructions to the Applicants: Position requires a valid Class E driver’s license. This position may involve driving to various locations on and off campus to conduct University business. The anticipated salary range for this position is $89,076 - $115,000. The final salary will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and internal equity considerations. All applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position, and the university cannot accommodate H‑1B transfers or employment-based visa processing for individuals currently sponsored by another employer. This role requires the successful candidate to work on-site at UCF as their primary work location. On-site presence is an essential function of this role. Are you ready to unleash YOUR potential? As a next-generation public research university and Forbes-ranked top employer in Florida, we are a community of thinkers, doers, creators, innovators, healers, and leaders striving to create broader prosperity and help shape a better future. No matter what your role is, when you join Knight Nation, you’ll play an integral role at one of the most impactful universities in the country. You’ll be met with opportunities to connect and collaborate with talented faculty, staff, and students across 12 colleges and multiple campuses, engaging in impactful work that makes a positive difference. Your time at UCF will provide you with many meaningful opportunities to grow, you’ll work alongside talented colleagues on complex projects that will challenge you and help you gain new skills, and you’ll have countless rewarding experiences that go well beyond a paycheck. Working at UCF has its perks! UCF offers: Benefit packages, including Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending, and Employee Assistance Program Paid time off, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays Retirement savings options Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions Education assistance And more…For more benefits information, view the UCF Employee Benefits Guide . Dive into our Total Rewards Calculator to discover the diverse selection available to you, giving you a glimpse into the benefits that together shape your comprehensive rewards package at UCF. Unless explicitly stated on the job posting, it is UCF’s expectation that an employee of UCF will reside in Florida as of the date the employment begins . Department UCF IT Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm Type of Appointment Regular Expected Salary $89,076.00 to Negotiable Job Posting End Date 10-14-2026-12-00-AM The University of Central Florida is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based on any characteristic protected by law.  The University maintains programs for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities in accordance with all applicable federal and state laws. As a Florida public university, the University of Central Florida makes all application materials and selection procedures available to the public upon request. UCF is proud to be a smoke-free campus and an E-Verify employer. For general application or posting questions, please email talent@ucf.edu . If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please email onac@ucf.edu . People Also Viewed Executive Director – NCTI Orlando Business Development and Partn (A&P) Information Security Professional IV, Lead Orlando Information Technology (A&P) Administrative Assista