      "title": "Post Doctoral Scholar",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Scholar - Orlando, Florida, United States University of Central Florida Navigation Home Meet Our People Featured Jobs Resources Faculty Join Our Talent Network Search Jobs Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Scholar Post Doc/Med Residents (Fac) Skip to section BENEFITS WHY UCF? ABOUT ORLANDO My Profile Ready to Apply? Post Doctoral Scholar R113273 Main Campus, Orlando, Florida Faculty Full time NanoScience Technology Center Add to favorites View favorites This postdoctoral research position is housed in a laboratory focused on clean energy and carbon neutrality, with an emphasis on high‑impact research in electrochemical energy conversion. The successful candidate will conduct advanced experimental research, contribute to scholarly publications in top-tier journals, and support the development of competitive research proposals for federal funding agencies. Experimental Research Design, synthesize, and evaluate advanced electrocatalysts (e.g., NiFeMo systems, spinel oxides) and integrate them into seawater electrolyzers, fuel cells, and battery platforms. Data Analysis and Publication Analyze complex electrochemical performance data, conduct comprehensive materials characterization, and prepare high‑quality manuscripts for submission to leading peer‑reviewed journals (e.g., Nature Communications ). Project Management Support the Principal Investigator in the preparation of research proposals (e.g., NSF DMR) and assist with the management of technical reports for ongoing clean energy research projects. Mentorship and Training Provide technical guidance and hands‑on training to graduate and undergraduate students, with particular emphasis on electrochemical reactor operation and laboratory safety protocols. Laboratory Operations and Maintenance Ensure the proper operation and maintenance of electrochemical workstations and oversee the procurement of specialized membranes, chemicals, and laboratory supplies. Department Office of Research - Nanoscience Technology Center (NTC) - Operations CG Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm. Schedule may vary as required Type of Appointment Fixed Term (Fixed Term) Expected Salary $57,000.00 As a Florida public university, the University of Central Florida makes all application materials and selection procedures available to the public upon request. UCF is proud to be a smoke-free campus and an E-Verify employer. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 407-823-1336 or email onac@ucf.edu . For general application or posting questions, please email talent@ucf.edu . People Also Viewed Executive Director – NCTI Orlando Business Development and Partn (A&P) Information Security Professional IV, Lead Orlando Information Technology (A&P) Administrative Assistant II Orlando Administrative Management and (USPS) Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! First Name (required) b488212e Last Name (required) 31a3bf94 Email (required) 281840c0 Phone Number 7c2e32f3 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243)